    <GaugingStation location="Byton" name="Lugg" number="55014">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V Crump profile weir. Runoff reduced by groundwater abstraction for PWS.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Some shoaling u/s. Multiple ratings applied through the period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V weir Crump profile weir, 1:20 cross-slopes, 12.5m wide constructed in 1971. Pre-1971, station was natural river section with stable riffle control. Above 2m left bank overtopped, right bank is steep cliff.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Ratings reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed from 1981. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Aquifer provides significant baseflow and moderates flood peaks. Runoff reduced by groundwater abstraction for PWS.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Headwaters drain Radnor Forest - underlain by Silurian bedrock. Impermeable formations are covered by extensive alluvial gravel deposits in the valleys. Predominantly grassland catchment supporting rough grazing, with some forestry.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">P</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Good fit to rating." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating does not account for non-modular conditions or out of bank flow." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
